--- doc/upvar.n
+++ doc/upvar.n
@@ -70,10 +70,24 @@
 \fBunset\fR operation affects the variable it is linked to, not the
 upvar variable.  There is no way to unset an upvar variable except
 by exiting the procedure in which it is defined.  However, it is
 possible to retarget an upvar variable by executing another \fBupvar\fR
 command.
+.PP
+If \fBupvar\fR is invoked outside of any procedure (at global level or
+inside \fBnamespace eval\fR), \fImyVar\fR is created as a variable of
+the current namespace instead of a local variable. Such a link persists
+until the namespace is deleted; unsetting \fImyVar\fR only unsets
+the variable it is linked to.
+.PP
+\fIOtherVar\fR may be a qualified name; it is resolved in the context of
+the frame given by \fIlevel\fR, following the usual rules described in
+\fBnamespace\fR(n).
+\fIMyVar\fR may also be a qualified name, even inside a procedure;
+then the link is created as a namespace variable. A relative qualified
+\fImyVar\fR is resolved relative to the current namespace only, and the
+namespace that contains it must already exist.
